WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:05.529
Game of Thrones Season 6 Episode 3 is out,
and there a heap to talk about so let’s

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:08.890
begin.
At the Wall, Jon Snow rises from the dead,

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:12.700
and people think he’s “the prince that
was promised”, or “Azor Ahai reborn”,

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:17.570
a messianic figure prophesied to save the
world from darkness – basically kind of

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:22.750
a Game of Thrones Jesus – and Jon is pretty
Jesus-y, isn’t he? A righteous man betrayed

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:27.779
by his friends, killed before a cross, risen
from the dead, great hair, sweet abs. It’s

00:00:27.779 --> 00:00:31.980
not super clear what being this saviour means,
but it seems to involve fighting the white

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:37.440
walkers and their wights. Also, Melisandre
asks Jon where he went and what he saw when

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.739
he was dead, and Jon says “nothing”. Mel
has a similar exchange with Beric Dondarrion

00:00:42.739 --> 00:00:48.070
when he’s resurrected three seasons ago. Maybe part of why Melisandre is so interested

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:53.399
in death is that she herself has been fleeing
death for apparently “several centuries”, maybe

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:58.920
she fears death, and that’s why she asks
about it so intently. Anyway the similarity

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.610
between Beric and Jon suggests that their
resurrections work by the same kinda magic.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:09.540
But when Beric is resurrected, he changes,
loses bits of his memories and identity. When

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:14.280
Jon comes back, all it takes is one of Davos’
legendary pep talks, and then he seems about

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:21.200
the same as he ever was. So is Jon truly unchanged
by death? Or will we see new sides to his

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.960
character this season?
Then we’re on a ship sailing south. We see

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:31.330
Gilly being cute, and Sam being not so cute.
The plan is for Sam to join the maesters at

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:35.640
the Citadel in Oldtown, which is sort of like
a university, where Sam can learn the knowledge

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:40.830
he needs to help the Watch – maybe he’ll
find some info on white walkers. But since

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:45.409
the Citadel doesn’t accept women, Sam will
be dropping Gilly and the baby off at Horn

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:49.770
Hill, with Sam’s family. He mentions his
mother Melessa is “kind”, and his sister

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:55.590
Talla is “lovely”, but his father Randyll
is neither. As Sam explained in Season 1,

00:01:55.590 --> 00:02:00.759
Randyll was horrible to Sam growing up – cursing,
caning, slapping and starving him to try to

00:02:00.759 --> 00:02:05.590
toughen him up into the strong, brave son
he wanted, instead of the soft, cowardly son

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:10.849
he got. Eventually Randyll threatened to kill
Sam unless he gave up his name and inheritance,

00:02:10.849 --> 00:02:15.549
which is how Sam ended up joining the Watch. And now Sam is coming home, bringing Gilly,

00:02:15.549 --> 00:02:20.529
and her baby, who they’re saying is Sam’s
when it’s actually Craster’s – Mance’s

00:02:20.529 --> 00:02:24.999
in the books cause there’s a baby-swap plot
– but the point is that this is gonna be

00:02:24.999 --> 00:02:30.059
an epically awkward Meet the Parents type
situation, except that De Niro is a battle-hardened

00:02:30.059 --> 00:02:34.730
war veteran, Ben Stiller is a fat Watchman
who killed an ice monster, and his girlfriend

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:42.010
is a wildling with an incest-baby, so this
is gonna go off. On another note, in the show,

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:46.260
Maester Aemon died last season at the Wall,
but in the books Maester Aemon comes along

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:51.319
with Sam and Gilly on this voyage, and he
dies on board the ship. There’s this beautiful

00:02:51.319 --> 00:02:56.459
moving scene with Aemon crying in the rain,
remembering his youth, depicted here by artist

00:02:56.459 --> 00:03:00.400
Kay Haung – see the link in the description
for more of his art.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:04.839
Then beyond the Wall, Bran has a vision of
the Tower of Joy. This event happened about

00:03:04.839 --> 00:03:09.419
twenty years ago, at the time of Robert’s
Rebellion, the war where Robert Baratheon

00:03:09.419 --> 00:03:14.689
took over Westeros from the Mad King Aerys
Targaryen, after the Mad King’s son Prince

00:03:14.689 --> 00:03:20.329
Rhaegar ran off with Ned Stark’s sister
Lyanna, who we saw as a child last episode.

00:03:20.329 --> 00:03:24.760
At this point in the war, both the Mad King,
and Prince Rhaegar have been killed, so Ned

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:29.419
Stark and a group of his men, including Meera
and Jojen’s father Howland Reed, have come

00:03:29.419 --> 00:03:34.549
looking for Lyanna at the Tower of Joy. They
find the Tower guarded by three Kingsguard

00:03:34.549 --> 00:03:39.120
– two Kingsguard in the show – including
the legendary swordsman Arthur Dayne – the

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.809
Sword of the Morning. They talk about the
war – the dialogue is kinda cooler in the

00:03:42.809 --> 00:03:47.939
books – and then they fight, with Dayne
pretty much kicking all their asses. He would’ve

00:03:47.939 --> 00:03:51.870
killed Ned too if Howland hadn’t stabbed
him in the back at the last moment, so that

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:57.459
Ned could finish Dayne off. It’s upsetting
for Bran to see his father act in this dishonourable

00:03:57.459 --> 00:04:02.739
way – Ned had this seemingly untouchable
reputation of honour and honesty , but if

00:04:02.739 --> 00:04:07.109
he didn’t tell the whole truth about what
happened with Dayne, what else might he have

00:04:07.109 --> 00:04:11.569
hidden? It’s also interesting to see Howland
wounded – maybe that’s related to why

00:04:11.569 --> 00:04:16.340
he hasn’t turned up yet in the series – cause
he is alive, at least in the books – he’s

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:20.509
the last living survivor of the Tower of Joy,
and people keep saying how great he is, but

00:04:20.509 --> 00:04:25.289
we still haven’t seen him. Maybe he was
disabled by this wound somehow and has to

00:04:25.289 --> 00:04:29.539
stay at home? Either way we’ll hopefully
see more of him soon, there are lots of cool

00:04:29.539 --> 00:04:35.000
theories about him. Anyway after the fight,
we start getting to the important bit – Ned

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:39.639
hears screaming from the Tower, which is presumably
Lyanna, because that’s who he came to find

00:04:39.639 --> 00:04:43.210
– but we don’t know what’s up – like,
is she in pain? is she dying? is she alone

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:48.379
up there? Just as we’re about to find out
the “raven” pulls Bran out of the vision.

00:04:48.379 --> 00:04:51.689
So it looks like we’ll have to wait a couple
more episodes to see what happened in the

00:04:51.689 --> 00:04:58.210
tower – but there are some huge old theories
about this – check out the R+L=J video for

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:01.800
details. But another thing we learn here is
that Bran can affect the past through his

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:07.680
visions – he calls out to Ned, and Ned hears
him. This could support the idea that Wylis

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:12.719
became Hodor when Bran somehow messed with
his mind in one of these visions, like, maybe

00:05:12.719 --> 00:05:18.389
Bran says Hodor to young Wylis, and that’s
where the name Hodor originally comes from,

00:05:18.389 --> 00:05:23.360
like some kinda timey-wimey Back to the Future
circular paradox type shit. And the point

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:28.370
of this for Bran’s character, could be to
show him the terrible potential of his power,

00:05:28.370 --> 00:05:33.439
to give him guilt, and the restraint, that
Bloodraven is trying to teach him. At the

00:05:33.439 --> 00:05:38.000
end of the scene Bran asks Bloodraven what
the point of all this training is and he vaguely

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:45.009
but dramatically says to learn everything.
Daenerys Targaryen arrives at Vaes Dothrak,

00:05:45.009 --> 00:05:50.090
the sacred city of the Dothraki, and she’s
actually been here before, way back Season

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:56.180
1, when she eats that horse heart. She meets
the dosh khaleen, the widows of dead khals,

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:00.469
who strip her and demean her and tell her
that that she may or may not be made to join

00:06:00.469 --> 00:06:04.879
their happy little retirement village, depending
on the results of a big meeting of all the

00:06:04.879 --> 00:06:09.710
Dothraki khalasars together. That might sound
bad for Dany – but having all the Dothraki

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:14.550
in one place with Dany’s dragon on the way
– might actually be an opportunity to take

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:20.169
control of a massive Dothraki army. This will
probably involve some Dothraki getting barbequed

00:06:20.169 --> 00:06:24.840
– and this this dosh khaleen woman is probably
first on Dany’s list.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:29.139
In Meereen, Varys questions Vala, the woman
we saw working with the Sons of the Harpy

00:06:29.139 --> 00:06:35.090
last season. Varys seems to play nice, offering
silver and passage to Pentos in return for

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:40.539
information on the Harpy. He says he doesn’t
torture and wouldn’t hurt a child. But is

00:06:40.539 --> 00:06:46.439
this really how Varys operates? We know he
lies, manipulates and kills – will he really

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:51.310
keep his promises to Valla, or will he dispose
of her once he has what he wants? There’s

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:56.139
a lot of moral complexity to Varys, at least
in the books – hopefully the show will reflect

00:06:56.139 --> 00:07:00.949
some of that. Anyway so Valla tells Varys
that the Sons of the Harpy are funded by three

00:07:00.949 --> 00:07:07.340
cities – Astapor, Yunkai and Volantis – which
makes sense, because those cities trade slaves,

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:12.259
and Dany banned slavery. When Varys tells
this to Tyrion, Missandei and Grey Worm, there’s

00:07:12.259 --> 00:07:15.979
talk of war between Meereen and these other
cities.

00:07:15.979 --> 00:07:20.749
In King’s Landing, we see the creepy Qyburn
with Varys’ spies, the children he calls

00:07:20.749 --> 00:07:26.419
“little birds”. In the books, these children
are mute – Varys has their tongues removed

00:07:26.419 --> 00:07:31.659
so they can’t share his secrets, but here,
the birds say Varys is nice, and gives him

00:07:31.659 --> 00:07:36.340
sweets, like a Santa Claus with no balls,
so yeah maybe the show is turning Varys into

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.539
more of a one-dimensional good guy, which
would be a shame. But the fact the “little

00:07:40.539 --> 00:07:44.219
birds” are included at all in the show hints
that they’ll play some future role – in

00:07:44.219 --> 00:07:49.430
fact that looks like them in the trailer murdering
a certain someone – for those who’ve read

00:07:49.430 --> 00:07:53.909
the books, that might be the scene at the
end of Dance. Then Cersei rolls in with her

00:07:53.909 --> 00:07:58.400
entourage of the one-handed Kingslayer and
the zombie-Mountain, she talks about wanting

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:03.469
to kill people, and she mentions the plans
to demand a trial by combat against the Faith,

00:08:03.469 --> 00:08:09.379
and that Robert Strong a.k.a. the Mountain
a.k.a. Gregor Clegane will fight for her.

00:08:09.379 --> 00:08:13.059
The question, then, is who the champion for
the Faith will be, who could possibly stand

00:08:13.059 --> 00:08:19.069
against Robert Strong? Well there is a theory
that a certain Gravedigger may rise to fight

00:08:19.069 --> 00:08:24.620
in what’s probably the most hyped hypothetical
fight in the fandom. It’ll be fucking crazy

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:29.629
if it happens, but probably more fun if it’s
a surprise, so let’s move on for now. Cersei

00:08:29.629 --> 00:08:34.060
and Jaime try to join the small council, but
Olenna Tyrell the Queen of Sick Burns talks

00:08:34.060 --> 00:08:39.010
smack about Cersei’s incest, Mace Tyrell
dithers, Pycelle farts, and Kevan leads the

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:45.060
council out of the room. This is the government
of Westeros, and it’s in a sorry bloody

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:49.870
state. At this point Kevan and maybe Olenna
are the only people really holding things

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:54.880
together. Then we see Tommen confront the
High Sparrow, all like ‘I’m an angry Lannister,

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.180
hear me roar, I make violent threats just
like my mum’, and the High Sparrow is like

00:08:59.180 --> 00:09:03.589
nah mate you’re not a lion, you’re a kitten,
now sit down, and let’s have a chat about

00:09:03.589 --> 00:09:08.089
Jesus, and Tommen’s like yeah okay let’s
do that. Try as he might, Tommen just isn’t

00:09:08.089 --> 00:09:12.730
intimidating or cruel like his parents, he’s
sensitive – and the Sparrow knows exactly

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:18.690
how to play him. Just like he undermines Cersei
by exploiting her pride and her body and sexuality,

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:23.430
and undermines Jaime by showing that his physical
power is useless, he controls Tommen by targeting

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:28.339
his insecurities about his relationship with
his mother, and his responsibilities as king.

00:09:28.339 --> 00:09:32.760
Tommen is a kid in need of guidance, in need
of a good father figure – the High Sparrow

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:39.500
sees this and provides – carefully drawing
Tommen in to his own ideology and control.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:46.440
The High Sparrow is not just a holy man – he’s
a master manipulator – so what’s his endgoal?

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:52.160
In Braavos, Arya gets a training montage – “Montage!”
She uses her senses to overcome her blindness,

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:57.079
she detects poisons by smell, she plays the
lying game and ultimately becomes a stronger

00:09:57.079 --> 00:10:01.519
person. She subtly threatens the waif, and
gives her a good smack in the face, so they’re

00:10:01.519 --> 00:10:06.470
really setting the groundwork here for conflict
between the two. Eventually a Man with Jaqen’s

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:09.930
face turns up and for the first time this
season we see this Jaqen and the waif together

00:10:09.930 --> 00:10:14.290
in the same room, showing that there are at
least two Faceless Men around, not just one

00:10:14.290 --> 00:10:18.970
swapping faces. In the books there seem to
be at least nine of them in total – maybe

00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:23.300
that’s true in the show as well. Anyway,
in the end, Arya gets her sight back. The

00:10:23.300 --> 00:10:28.660
blind part of training is over and she’s
ready to go kick arse. Whose arse, we don’t

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:32.709
yet know.
Then Lord Smalljon Umber turns up at Winterfell.

00:10:32.709 --> 00:10:36.509
He’s there to join up with Ramsay, but he
doesn’t kneel, doesn’t swear oaths, he

00:10:36.509 --> 00:10:41.589
calls Ramsay’s dad a coont and sees right
through his lies, so right away Ramsay’s

00:10:41.589 --> 00:10:47.269
rightly suspicious of this guy – why should
he trust him? Umber gives Ramsay a gift – Rickon,

00:10:47.269 --> 00:10:51.600
the youngest Stark brother, who everyone forgot
about, and Osha, the wildling who protected

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:56.779
him after they split from Bran. Since everyone
thinks Bran is dead, Rickon is the last known

00:10:56.779 --> 00:11:02.290
surviving male Stark, making him the rightful
Lord of Winterfell – and a very valuable

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:07.779
captive for Ramasy – especially after losing
Sansa. To show that the kid really is Rickon,

00:11:07.779 --> 00:11:13.889
Umber presents the head of Shaggydog, Rickon’s
direwolf, which… is really sad. Shaggy was

00:11:13.889 --> 00:11:18.190
there for Rickon when no one else was, he
represents Rickon’s anger and wildness,

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:22.949
and he showed so much promise – in the books
there’s a vision of Shaggy fighting a unicorn

00:11:22.949 --> 00:11:27.490
on Skagos, people hoped to see Rickon ride
Shaggydog into battle at Winterfell – this

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:33.009
wolf was just really metal and cool so it’s
sad to see him go. But it is funny that, in

00:11:33.009 --> 00:11:37.920
storytelling, a shaggy dog story is a long
story that ends up being pointless or anticlimactic,

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:43.470
so arguably Shaggydog himself is a sort of
a shaggydog story. Unless it’s not really

00:11:43.470 --> 00:11:47.910
Shaggy – some people have pointed out that
the head looks kinda small for a direwolf,

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:51.880
so maybe it’s just a normal wolf’s head,
and the Umbers are secretly still loyal to

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:56.600
the Starks – but this might just be wishful
thinking, cause in the second trailer, that

00:11:56.600 --> 00:12:01.160
is an Umber banner flying with the Bolton
army. So if anyone’s up to any Northern

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:05.089
conspiracy shenanigans it’ll probably be
the Manderleys, who Ramsay mentioned in the

00:12:05.089 --> 00:12:09.839
last episode. Those guys have some of the
best lines in the series, so get keen for

00:12:09.839 --> 00:12:14.649
that. But in the meantime, things don’t
look good for Rickon and Osha.

00:12:14.649 --> 00:12:18.649
Back at the Wall, Jon Snow kills the people
who killed him – a kind of revenge that

00:12:18.649 --> 00:12:23.120
not many people get to have. It’s actually
kinda cool that Jon hangs them, because if

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:29.160
Jon Snow is Jesus, these guys are like Judas,
and in the Bible, Judas hangs himself , depending

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:32.850
on which passage you read , it’s probably
a coincidence, but still a cool connection.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:36.750
Anyway it’s hard not to respect Alliser
for standing up for what he believed until

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:41.750
the very end. He just wanted to protect the
Watch. And Olly – lotta people wanted to

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:46.410
see Olly dead – jokingly mostly, but still
– it’s hard to be happy about a dead kid

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:51.230
isn’t it? The tragedy of all this drama
on the Wall is while these good men squabble

00:12:51.230 --> 00:12:56.819
amongst themselves, much greater threats lie
just to the south and north. These are the

00:12:56.819 --> 00:13:02.120
real enemies, and right now the Watch isn’t
anywhere near ready. Anyway after killing

00:13:02.120 --> 00:13:07.410
his killers, Jon hands command to Edd, and
says his watch is over. Mic drop. The vows

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:11.490
of the Night’s Watch say “it shall not
end until my death”, and since Jon died,

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:15.970
he’s now seen as freed from his vows, which
is kind of a bullshit technicality, maybe

00:13:15.970 --> 00:13:20.339
this could be seen as breaking his oath hashtag
episode title, but either way, it looks like

00:13:20.339 --> 00:13:24.829
we’re finally getting what’s been wanted
for a long while – Jon’s gonna ride south

00:13:24.829 --> 00:13:28.240
to Winterfell.
So this episode wasn’t as massive as the

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:33.399
last two – no resurrections, great revelations,
dead kings or destroyed houses – but there’s

00:13:33.399 --> 00:13:38.649
a lot of set-up here for future conflict.
There’s talk of war in Slaver’s Bay, Dany’s

00:13:38.649 --> 00:13:42.839
threatening the dosh khaleen with a dragon’s
on the way, a trial by combat is coming in

00:13:42.839 --> 00:13:47.410
King’s Landing, and most terrifying of all,
Sam’s bringing his girlfriend home to his

00:13:47.410 --> 00:13:51.370
parents. Bran’s getting stroppy with his
teacher, Arya’s getting stroppy with her

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:56.139
teacher, the Boltons have Rickon, and Jon
Snow’s watch is ended.

00:13:56.139 --> 00:13:59.589
Thank you for watching, please like and subscribe
if you’d like to see more, and thank you

00:13:59.589 --> 00:14:04.329
to all Patrons supporting the channel, including
Sarah Cleary, Spencer Bentley, Ryan Steele,

00:14:04.329 --> 00:14:08.310
Sid Yadav, William Armstrong, Amy cobb, Dcxalius
and G. Cheers.

